{#
  chat/wing-right.njk — the live-status wing, included AFTER the player.

  Context it reads:
    chatTitle   the film's title

  The screen has to answer "why can't I talk?" without anyone asking. The
  badge, the time left and the message say it together. The Focus button sits
  at the bottom, away from the reading order — it is the host's, and the room
  should not read it as something it is meant to press.

  Between the two sits "Ways to Take Part": read while the room is muted, so
  people reach the discussion already knowing how they can join it. The four
  are ways, not levels — listening is a whole way to take part, and nothing
  here ranks one person above another. On a short wing the explanations give
  way first and the four names stay; shorter still, the section goes and the
  status keeps the box (chatstatus container queries in chat-session.css).
  In the one-column fallback the four names sit under the status, and in
  Focus transcript the stage never gets too short to hold them (the floor in
  chat-session.js).

  Live values are written by js/chat-session.js through [data-chat] hooks,
  never by id, because the badge, the time-left line and the message each
  appear TWICE — once here, once in the narrow-screen band — and only one of
  the two is displayed at a given width. One selector updates both.
#}
<aside class="chat-wing chat-wing--right" aria-label="Session status">
    <div class="chat-status">
        <p class="chat-mic" data-chat="mic" data-state="muted" role="status">
            <span class="chat-mic-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="chat-mic-text" data-chat="mic-text">Visitor mics off</span>
        </p>
        <p class="chat-status-title" data-chat="title">{{ chatTitle }}</p>
        <div class="chat-meter" role="presentation">
            <div class="chat-meter-fill" data-chat="meter"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="chat-timeleft" data-chat="timeleft">Starting shortly</p>
        {#- The noun is per page and is set here as well as in chat-session.js,
            so the box reads correctly in the moment before the script runs —
            and still reads correctly if it never does. A ninety-second reading
            is a "short video"; the Creation film is not. -#}
        <p class="chat-message" data-chat="message">All visitor mics are turned off while this {{ chatMicNoun | default("short video") }} plays. Mics will be turned on at the end for Q/A + discussion.</p>
    </div>
    <section class="chat-ways" aria-labelledby="chatWaysTitle">
        <h2 class="chat-ways-title" id="chatWaysTitle">Ways to Take Part</h2>
        <ul class="chat-ways-list">
            <li><span class="chat-ways-name">Listen &middot; Ask</span> <span class="chat-ways-text">an honest question before responding in turn.</span></li>
            <li><span class="chat-ways-name">Participate &middot; Share</span> <span class="chat-ways-text">your understanding. Explore relevant scripture, teachings, experience, or reasoning.</span></li>
            <li><span class="chat-ways-name">Relate &middot; Connect</span> <span class="chat-ways-text">your understanding to the perspectives of others. Identify where understandings agree or differ.</span></li>
            <li><span class="chat-ways-name">Integrate &middot; Deepen</span> <span class="chat-ways-text">your own perspectives. Summarize what you have learned. Consider what it means to live your faith within your communities.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <div class="chat-wing-controls">
        {#- A film normally shown in part gets a switch. It sits with Focus at
            the bottom of the box, at the same quiet weight: both are the
            host's, and the room should not read either as something it is
            meant to press. The view pair is chat/view-pair.njk. -#}
        {% if chatParts %}<button class="chat-mode-btn" type="button" data-chat="mode">&#8644; Part 1 only</button>{% endif %}
        {% include "chat/view-pair.njk" %}
    </div>
</aside>
